Chapter: YahtzeeWasm
  cites Games chapter Yahtzee
  cites Games chapter Rng
  cites Foreword chapter List

 The browser interface for Yahtzee, on the handle contract in
 games-backlog.md GAME-11. Two thirteen-entry cards and five dice are past
 an i32, so the page holds the state's address.

 `yh-do-turn` writes the scorecard with `list-set-at`, which mutates in
 place, so `yh-wasm-turn` copies first.

 Scoring is exposed on five loose dice rather than on the state, because
 the whole scoring table is decidable over the 7,776 dice combinations and
 a grader wants to ask about all of them, not about the ones a game rolled.

 We say:

Section: Copying

  yh-copy-13 : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  yh-copy-13 (src) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 13 then acc
    else yh-copy-13 src (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at src i))

  yh-copy-dice : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  yh-copy-dice (src) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= list-length src then acc
    else yh-copy-dice src (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at src i))

  yh-copy-state : YahtzeeState -> YahtzeeState
  yh-copy-state (s) =
    YahtzeeState {
      scorecard = yh-copy-13 (s.scorecard) 0 [],
      scored    = yh-copy-13 (s.scored) 0 [],
      dice      = yh-copy-dice (s.dice) 0 [],
      rng       = s.rng
    }

Section: Scoring, on Loose Dice

  yh-five : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  yh-five (a) (b) (c) (d) (e) =
    list-push (list-push (list-push (list-push (list-push [] a) b) c) d) e

  yh-wasm-score : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  yh-wasm-score (a) (b) (c) (d) (e) (cat) =
    if cat < 0 then (-1)
    else if cat >= 13 then (-1)
    else yh-score-category (yh-five a b c d e) cat

  yh-wasm-best-cat : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  yh-wasm-best-cat (a) (b) (c) (d) (e) =
    yh-ai-pick-category (yh-five a b c d e) (yh-build-zeroes 13 []) (yh-build-zeroes 13 [])

Section: The Browser Interface

  yh-wasm-new : Integer -> YahtzeeState
  yh-wasm-new (seed) = yh-init seed

  yh-wasm-card : YahtzeeState, Integer -> Integer
  yh-wasm-card (s) (cat) =
    if cat < 0 then (-1)
    else if cat >= 13 then (-1)
    else list-at (s.scorecard) cat

  yh-wasm-scored : YahtzeeState, Integer -> Integer
  yh-wasm-scored (s) (cat) =
    if cat < 0 then (-1)
    else if cat >= 13 then (-1)
    else list-at (s.scored) cat

  yh-wasm-die : YahtzeeState, Integer -> Integer
  yh-wasm-die (s) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= list-length (s.dice) then (-1)
    else list-at (s.dice) i

  yh-wasm-total : YahtzeeState -> Integer
  yh-wasm-total (s) = yh-total-score (s.scorecard) 0 0

  yh-wasm-turn : YahtzeeState -> YahtzeeState
  yh-wasm-turn (s) = yh-do-turn (yh-copy-state s)

Section: Playing By Hand

 `yh-do-turn` rolls three times, picks its own keeps and chooses its own
 category, all in one call, so a person cannot get inside it. These are the
 same steps taken one at a time.

 HOW MANY ROLLS ARE LEFT IS NOT KEPT HERE. It is a fact about the turn in
 progress, not about the game, and `YahtzeeState` has no room for it without
 a new field on a record built in five places. The page counts the rolls, the
 same way it holds which square you have picked up in every other game.

 The keep mask arrives as five BITS rather than a list, because a browser
 hands over one integer: bit i set means die i is held and does not roll
 again. The engine's own `yh-reroll-some` reads a list where 1 means keep,
 so `yh-keep-list` is the only translation.

  yh-keep-list : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  yh-keep-list (bits) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 5 then acc
    else yh-keep-list (bits / 2) (i + 1) (list-push acc (rng-mod bits 2))

  yh-wasm-roll : YahtzeeState -> YahtzeeState
  yh-wasm-roll (s) =
    let st = yh-copy-state s
    in let r = rng-next (st.rng)
    in YahtzeeState { scorecard = st.scorecard, scored = st.scored,
                      dice = yh-roll-dice r, rng = r }

  yh-wasm-reroll : YahtzeeState, Integer -> YahtzeeState
  yh-wasm-reroll (s) (keep) =
    if keep < 0 then s
    else if keep > 31 then s
    else let st = yh-copy-state s
    in let r = rng-next (st.rng)
    in let mask = yh-keep-list keep 0 []
    in YahtzeeState { scorecard = st.scorecard, scored = st.scored,
                      dice = yh-reroll-some (st.dice) mask r, rng = r }

 Scoring the dice you are holding into a category you have not used. A
 category already spent is refused rather than overwritten: in Yahtzee a
 filled box is filled for the rest of the game, and a caller that ignores
 the refusal would otherwise silently rewrite a score.

  yh-wasm-take : YahtzeeState, Integer -> YahtzeeState
  yh-wasm-take (s) (cat) =
    if cat < 0 then s
    else if cat > 12 then s
    else if list-at (s.scored) cat == 1 then s
    else let st = yh-copy-state s
    in let sc = yh-score-category (st.dice) cat
    in YahtzeeState { scorecard = list-set-at (st.scorecard) cat sc,
                      scored = list-set-at (st.scored) cat 1,
                      dice = st.dice, rng = st.rng }

 What a category WOULD score with the dice on the table. Yahtzee is a game
 of choosing where to spend a roll, and choosing without this is guesswork
 rather than play.

  yh-wasm-preview : YahtzeeState, Integer -> Integer
  yh-wasm-preview (s) (cat) =
    if cat < 0 then (-1)
    else if cat > 12 then (-1)
    else yh-score-category (s.dice) cat

  yh-wasm-filled : YahtzeeState -> Integer
  yh-wasm-filled (s) = yh-count-filled (s.scored) 0 0

  yh-count-filled : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  yh-count-filled (sc) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= 13 then acc
    else yh-count-filled sc (i + 1) (acc + list-at sc i)

Section: The Whole Game

  yh-wasm-run : Integer -> YahtzeeResult
  yh-wasm-run (seed) = run-yahtzee-game seed

  yh-wasm-res-score : YahtzeeResult -> Integer
  yh-wasm-res-score (r) = r.final-score

  yh-wasm-res-turns : YahtzeeResult -> Integer
  yh-wasm-res-turns (r) = r.turns-taken

